  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 1504.04 Department Processing of Pre-approval Requests",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 1504.04 Department Processing of Pre-approval Requests.\n\n(a) Pre-approval requests shall be processed in the order in which they are received.\n\n(b) If the department determines that a pre-approval request does not contain all required information pursuant to Env-Dw 1504.02, the department shall notify the applicant in writing within 30 days specifying the information required for a complete request. The department shall not process incomplete pre-approval requests.\n\n(c) In response to being notified of department determination, an applicant may modify or supplement information and submit a new pre-approval request to the department.\n\n(d) If the department determines that a pre-approval request contains all required information pursuant to Env-Dw 1504.02, the department shall continue to process the request.\n\n(e) The department shall determine whether the applicant is income qualified pursuant to Env-Dw 1503.03(a) within 60 days.\n\n(f) If the department determines that the applicant is income qualified pursuant to Env-Dw 1503.03(a), the department shall grant written pre-approval to the applicant to request a rebate under Env-Dw 1505 be distributed directly to a treatment installer or contractor.\n\n(g) If the department determines the applicant is not income qualified pursuant to Env-Dw 1503.03(a), the department shall not grant pre-approval and shall notify the applicant of the reason(s) for such determination in writing.\n\nSource. #14201, eff 2-26-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw1500.html"
}
